(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/config.asl#" :text "Pure AgentSlang Gateway Configuration Parser, Calibration Index Ingestion, and Intent Router ported from bin/asl-gateway")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/config.asl#GatewayProvider.kind" :text "openai (default: OpenAI-compatible chat/completions or /responses, Authorization: Bearer), cli (agy/codex/claude, no HTTP), anthropic (POST {base}/messages in the Anthropic Messages shape, x-api-key + anthropic-version headers; needs :base like openai does), or gemini (POST {base}/models/{model}:generateContent in the Gemini generateContent shape, same Authorization: Bearer as openai; needs :base like openai does; the model name rides in the URL path, not the body). Example: (:provider :id commandCodeMsg :kind anthropic :base \"https://api.commandcode.ai/provider/v1\" :keyEnv COMMANDCODE_API_KEY) (:provider :id opencodeGemini :kind gemini :base \"https://opencode.ai/inference/go/v1\" :keyEnv OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY :sessionHeader \"x-opencode-session\")")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/config.asl#GatewayPool" :text "batch: the upstream takes one POST of {\"batch\": [bodies]}; scaleDownPath: POSTed once a pool drains")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/config.asl#RetryPolicy" :text ":retry (:max N :baseMs N :capMs N) on a (:provider ...) or (:model ...): a transient upstream failure on that model (a 429 whose body reads as a per-model rate limit or overload, not a provider-wide quota/billing marker; 502/503/504; a connection reset or timeout) retries the SAME model up to :max extra times with full-jitter exponential backoff (:baseMs doubling per attempt, capped at :capMs, or the upstream's Retry-After header when present) before any cascade to the next model or circuit-breaker trip. A model's own :retry wins over its provider's; absent on both, :max is 0 and nothing about today's behaviour changes. No environment variable controls this: every knob is a config row.")
