(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/config.asl#gatewayDecideLoad!" :text "gatewayDecidePoint over the file at path; a missing file is the static default plus a reason")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/sessions.asl#" :text "GW-SESSIONS-2: a gateway session is a named handle onto a vendor CLI's own conversation id; each turn runs the vendor headless through fleet/run runGuarded (no tmux, no pty) and continues the same context with the vendor's resume flag. Ops: asl gateway session start|send|list|show|stop|forget take one ASN property list and print one ASN receipt (start :name :vendor :cwd :args :text; send :name :text [:args]). Rows are one file per session, ~/.asl/run/sessions/NAME.asn (0600, dir 0700) plus NAME.reply; a symlink NAME.lock whose target is the owner pid allows one turn at a time (second concurrent op is (:err :code busy), a lock whose owner died is taken over); stop kills the lock owner's process tree. cwd must be absolute without #. The child env is PATH HOME LANG LC_ALL LC_CTYPE TERM USER TMPDIR plus the vendor row's :env names. Flags live only in ~/.asl/gateway.asn: (:gateway :sessionsTimeoutSec N :sessions ((:vendor N :bin B :first (ARGS) :resume (ARGS with {id}) :sep S :idFrom KEY :replyFrom KEY :wrap TEMPLATE :wrapResume TEMPLATE :env (NAME ...)) ...)); argv is bin, first-or-resume head, extra args, then the prompt (after :sep, or as {prompt} in a wrap template). An absent row refuses every start.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/sessions.asl#sessKeyValues" :text "values of a key in vendor output in order: JSON \"key\": value and ASN :key value")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/sessions.asl#sessLock!" :text "symlink lock NAME.lock to OWNERPID:NONCE: creation is atomic so exactly one turn runs per session; the token proves ownership, a stale lock is taken over by renaming it to a unique name and re-reading it, and unlock/finish only act while the lock still holds the token")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/sessions.asl#vendorDefaults" :text "flags checked against local help and keys confirmed by one real headless call per vendor (2026-10-25): claude -p --output-format json, resume --resume ID, id key session_id, reply key result, --model M, fork via --resume ID --fork-session; codex exec --json --skip-git-repo-check, resume codex exec resume --json --skip-git-repo-check ID PROMPT, id key thread_id (thread.started event), reply = last text (item.completed agent_message), -m M, no headless fork (codex fork is interactive); agy --output-format json with -p PROMPT, resume --conversation ID, id key conversation_id, reply key response, usage object input_tokens output_tokens cache_read_tokens, --model M; leon runs asl '(:agent :task P :resume S)' and reads :session. The sample row is sampleConfig in tests/sessionsTest.asl")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#" :text "GW-SESSION-BIND: caller-session binding for CLI vendors. Caller key: header X-ASL-Session first (the server fallback asl-run-* is ignored), else body field session; the body field user is not a key. Trust model (loopback single-user gateway): the caller key is the bearer key of the request and there are no gateway-issued tokens in this round; it is hashed at once and never stored, logged or written to the ledger. Every binding lives under b-<sha256 prefix 24> in the session store with kind binding; named sessions may not start with b-, send refuses a binding, and a binding never resumes a row that is not kind binding (error namespace). The row holds vendor, model, vendor session id, delivered message count, a digest of the delivered messages (length-prefixed role/text pairs, tool_calls and tool_call_id text included, the assistant reply as the client received it after sanitizing) and a context digest of the system prompt text and cwd. Resume only when vendor, model and context digest are unchanged, the binding is inside :sessionsTtlSec (0 = none), and the digest of the first N request messages equals the row digest; the vendor then gets only the new messages with its resume flag. Every other case replays the whole transcript into a fresh vendor session and the receipt says (:resumed false :why noBinding|vendorSwitch|modelSwitch|contextChanged|expired|noVendorSession|diverged|noNewMessage); the HTTP response carries it as asl.binding. Each turn, success or failure, appends exactly one gatewayCalls ledger row (api cliBinding, alias and tag binding:NAME, file 0600). Ops: asl gateway session list|bindings, show :name or :key, forget/stop, fork :name :to (needs :fork args in the vendor row, claude --fork-session). Stop kills only the vendor child named in the lease (verified child of the lock owner and group leader), never the lock owner, so forgetting a binding with a turn in flight cannot kill the gateway; the turn then stores nothing. One turn per binding at a time (busy)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#boundCliEffect!" :text "live chat entry for bindings: chat.asl cliDispatch adds :session (caller key), :messages and :sanitize to the effCli arguments only when the request has a caller key; server.asl drive! serves such an effect when the client is in the sessions allowlist of gateway.asn, otherwise the effect is unchanged. The reactor does not block: boundCliBegin! spawns the vendor through fleet/run guardStart! and the connection parks in connCli; every reactor turn boundAdvance! pumps the child and judges its limits (poll timeout 50 ms while one is parked), and the continuation resumes when the child ends, so other requests are served meanwhile (tests/boundReactorTest.asl asserts the order). runEffect! keeps a blocking path for callers outside the reactor. The bound turn keeps the dispatch policy: cliBoundFlags! runs the claude/codex/agy builders (system prompt file, tool lean flags, model, effort) and removes by flag name what the session row supplies (headless, json output, the prompt) and what stops the vendor keeping its conversation (claude --no-session-persistence, codex --ephemeral); the per-turn temp dir is 0700 and removed when the turn ends or is killed; system messages are the system prompt (part of the context digest) and not of the delivered transcript. execSec is seconds. Verified by tests/boundChatTest.asl, bindingFixTest.asl, boundReactorTest.asl")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#bindCtxDigest" :text "sha256 of the length-prefixed system prompt text and cwd a binding was started under; a different value forces a replay (contextChanged)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#bindDecide" :text "resume decision for a binding row: resume only when vendor, model, context digest, TTL and delivered-prefix digest all match, else a replay naming why")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#bindDigest" :text "sha256 of a message list, each role and text length-prefixed so no text can imitate a boundary")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#BindPlan" :text "decision result: resume flag, why, vendor session id to resume and the prompt to send")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#bindRender" :text "renders messages as the vendor prompt: one user message bare, otherwise role-labelled blocks")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#BMsg" :text "a delivered message: role and text (tool_calls and tool_call_id included in text)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#boundAdvance!" :text "steps a parked bound turn once without blocking; returns the finished result when the vendor has ended, else the updated pending turn")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#boundBegin!" :text "starts a bound turn: takes the binding lock, decides resume or replay and spawns the vendor without waiting; failures return boundDone")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#boundChat!" :text "blocking bound turn rendered as an ASN receipt")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#boundChatBody!" :text "bound turn from a chat request body and header key; the key is header then body session, never body user")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#BoundCli" :text "start result of a bound CLI effect: boundCliNow with the reply or none, or boundCliRunning with the pending turn")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#boundCliBegin!" :text "starts a bound CLI effect with the dispatch policy flags (cliBoundFlags!) without waiting")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#boundCliEligible?" :text "true when the effect carries a caller key and the client is in the sessions allowlist")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/binding.asl#boundCliFinish" :text "turns a finished bound result into the chat CliReply (none on failure)")
